{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>שלח</b> — it follows the sense of <b>שלח</b> in a decree." "<b>מלך</b> — he is the king of Egypt, and [it means] he opened him from the fetters."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 105, :notes {0 "The comment is terse and syntactically compressed; 'ישרת אחר טעם' likely means 'it follows after [i.e., conforms to] the sense of.' The referent of the comparison (another occurrence of שלח meaning a royal decree) is left unspecified by Ibn Ezra.", 1 "Hebrew 'ויפתחהו' is parsed as the hifil of פתח with a 3ms pronominal suffix; translated hyper-literally."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:38:28.581709730Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}